  "body": "What happens: the Heidenhain DIN/ISO post has three small output faults.\n1. `ff` rounds each F word to a whole mm/min. A feed under 0.5 mm/min becomes `F0`.\n2. `G207` accepts a set-up clearance of 0 and writes `Q200=+0`. The tap then has no distance to accelerate before it cuts.\n3. `clean()` keeps the tilde (`~`) in the setup, operation and tool notes. The shared `commentText` and the Klartext `cleanText` remove it. HEIDENHAIN uses `~` as a block continuation mark. No case was found where a note line ends with `~` (the `*` follows it), so this is a consistency fix.\n\nExpected:\n1. Write a decimal feed, or refuse a feed that rounds to 0 by name.\n2. Warn when `G207` has `Q200=0`. The R plane is the user's choice, so do not refuse it.\n3. `clean()` removes `~`, as `commentText` does.\n\nEvidence (upstream/main `1c0152c91`):\n- `assets/posts/heidenhain.cps:76` (`ff`) and `:90` (`fw`).\n- `heidenhain.cps:801` (a clearance of 0 is accepted) and `:815` (`Q200`). Golden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/heidenhain/tap_plate.nc`, block N100: `G207 Q200=+0`.\n- `heidenhain.cps:207-211` (`clean`). Compare `crates/post/src/post/js_host.rs:99-101` and `assets/posts/heidenhain-klartext.cps:36-38`.\n- HEIDENHAIN TNC 640 cycle programming manual (ID 892905-25), cycle 207.\n\nFound by the post audit against the HEIDENHAIN manuals (#4130).\n\nDone means:\n- No feed in the allowed range posts `F0`.\n- `G207` with `Q200=0` gives a warning.\n- No note keeps `~`.\n- A test pins each item.\n",
